the city of castle in the German state  of Heston has hosted the documenter art  exhibition since its inception in 1955  but this year castle will share that  honor with a city located almost 3,000  kilometers away athens in april the huge  art show will kick off in greece the  first time ever it's opened outside of  Germany documentas artistic director  Adams Tim chicks controversial decision  is a show of solidarity with the city  bearing the brunt of both the economic  crisis and the refugee crisis documenta  is once again coming in for criticism  some say it's view of art is to cerebral  with too many works tackling political  themes at the expense of true artistic  sensibility Nadia Akira pelu a curator  in Athens independent art scene is just  a little nervous about whether Athens  can put it off my biggest concern is  that believe it or not that documenta  will fail we may be critical with it but  we are curious and we wanted to succeed  because we will be left with the post  coitus melancholia architect and  documentary artist Andreas and Gary  darkest says Athens is already the  winner only the most important capital  that documenta is donating to Athens is  is attention because that is something  that you you know you are here making a  documentary other institutions are  interested in doing something in Athens  because documenta is there they want to  share that attention and of course they  generate more so I think that's very  valuable backing Castle another artist  is also directing attention towards  athens Marta minhwan from Argentina will  create a replica of the Parthenon from  100,000 banned books the work is a  protest against the censorship of free  speech
 

